Enginehost: a window icon the game does not ship is not a fatal error.

Ren'Py 8.x's set_icon loads config.window_icon (gui/window_icon.png in the
gui template) the first time the display starts, and only a web download is
caught, so a game without that file stopped at its first line of dialogue
(rig, tracker#411). A handheld has no window icon to set; skip it.
--- a/renpy/display/core.py
+++ b/renpy/display/core.py
@@ -1070,5 +1070,8 @@
                 pygame.display.set_icon(im)
             except renpy.webloader.DownloadNeeded:
                 pass
+            except Exception as e:
+                # Enginehost: a missing or unreadable icon leaves the window without one.
+                renpy.display.log.write("Window icon %r not set: %r", icon, e)

     def set_window_caption(self, force=False):
